  What:the spine,desc:Peeroleum — an envelope with a seq and an ack — a Pier per peer with an outbox and an inbox — every frame books an unemit served under the beliefs mutex
    Doc:Ghost/N/Peeroleum.g
    Point,method:Peeroleum_send,desc:outbound — allocate seq — book the emit — hand to the carrier
    Point,method:Peeroleum_deliver,desc:inbound gate — timing dose — calls deliver_do
    Point,method:Peeroleum_deliver_do,desc:route by header — ack ping pulse fast paths — book the unemit — pier-less roads
    Point,method:req_unemit,desc:the inbox worker — dispatch a booked frame to its handler — ack or fault
    Point,method:Peeroleum_take_ack,desc:an ack retires an emit — hello and trust acked here too
    Point,method:Peeroleum_on,desc:register an app handler for a frame type on this world
    Point,method:Peeroleum_route,desc:header.to → Peering + Pier
    Point,method:Peeroleum_bound_inbox,desc:the cap — shed and whittle so an inbox never grows without bound
  What:the handshake,desc:say and hear — hello then trust — a Ud is the pre-trust gate on the inbox
    Doc:Ghost/N/Peeroleum.g
    Point,method:say_hello,desc:first word to a Pier — once — seq from Pier_next_seq
    Point,method:hear_hello,desc:verify the pubkey matches the Pier — reply hello — mint the Ud
    Point,method:say_trust,desc:the second word — trust everything v1
    Point,method:hear_trust,desc:accept trust — the Pier is ready
    Point,method:Peeroleum_peer_ready,desc:handshake complete? — gates app frames
    Point,method:Peeroleum_reset_handshake,desc:a reborn peer — drop protocol outbox inbox faulty and start over
  What:the carriers,desc:Tribunal — the real websocket to the relay with auto-reconnect and backoff — mock and webrtc beside it
    Doc:Ghost/N/Tribunal.g
    Point,method:Socket_real,desc:the websocket carrier — dial reconnect bulk lane control frames hello_ok fan-out
    Point,method:Socket,desc:the mock carrier — loopback for Books
    Point,method:Tribunal_activate_websocket,desc:stamp the active transport on the world
    Point,method:Tribunal_fall_to_websocket,desc:webrtc failed — fall back
    Point,method:Tribunal_redial,desc:a Peering whose socket died — when to try again
    Doc:src/lib/server/relay.ts
    Point,method:attachRelay,desc:the relay — locals map — bind by addr role or hello — r2r bridge to the other dev server
    Point,method:deliverLocal,desc:own-door rule — a socket that dialled or declared the address is the door
    Point,method:handleHello,desc:signed identity bind — the seat arbiter — want and grant
    Point,method:routeFromBrowser,desc:deliver local else forward once over the bridge
    Point,method:dialEditor,desc:the runner relay dials the editor relay — one peerLink — last dialer wins
    Doc:src/lib/p2p/pinned_stable/Tribunal.go
